From: losos <losos@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:53:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] QIconLoader: Keep the system icon theme whatever the
 application sets

While the system names an icon theme (QT_QPA_SYSTEM_ICON_THEME or the
platform theme), QIcon::setThemeName() with another name no longer
replaces it; the requested theme becomes the fallback instead, unless the
application set one, so icons only it has still resolve. KDE Frameworks'
KIconTheme asks for Breeze this way on every desktop but Plasma. An empty
name still clears it.

The theme search path starts with the system's directories, whatever
QIcon::setThemeSearchPaths() was given, so an application can neither
shadow the system theme with a directory of the same name nor drop the
directories it lives in.
---
 src/gui/image/qiconloader.cpp | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gui/image/qiconloader.cpp b/src/gui/image/qiconloader.cpp
index 62353ec9..33daefff 100644
--- a/src/gui/image/qiconloader.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/image/qiconloader.cpp
@@ -159,6 +159,22 @@ QString QIconLoader::themeName() const
 
 void QIconLoader::setThemeName(const QString &themeName)
 {
+    // The icon theme is the desktop's choice, not the application's: while
+    // the system names one, an application asking for another (KDE apps ask
+    // for Breeze off Plasma) keeps the system's. Its theme still fills in
+    // icons the system's lacks, as the fallback, unless it chose one itself.
+    // Clearing the name with an empty string works as before.
+    if (!themeName.isEmpty()) {
+        const QString system = systemThemeName();
+        if (!system.isEmpty()) {
+            qCDebug(lcIconLoader) << "Keeping the system icon theme" << system << "over" << themeName;
+            if (m_userFallbackTheme.isEmpty() && themeName != system) {
+                m_userFallbackTheme = themeName;
+                invalidateKey();
+            }
+            return;
+        }
+    }
     if (m_userTheme == themeName)
         return;
 
@@ -201,7 +217,16 @@ QStringList QIconLoader::themeSearchPaths() const
         // Always add resource directory as search path
         m_iconDirs.append(":/icons"_L1);
     }
-    return m_iconDirs;
+    // The system's directories come first, in their own order, whatever the
+    // application set: otherwise it could shadow the system theme with a
+    // directory of the same name, or drop the system's directories and with
+    // them the theme. The application's own directories follow.
+    QStringList dirs = systemIconSearchPaths();
+    for (const QString &dir : std::as_const(m_iconDirs)) {
+        if (!dirs.contains(dir))
+            dirs.append(dir);
+    }
+    return dirs;
 }
 
 void QIconLoader::setFallbackSearchPaths(const QStringList &searchPaths)
-- 
2.43.0

